        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "dff7969a-27d0-3249-987e-3f33953f3282",
                "word": "pétaudière",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "497ae6ba-ea27-4a5e-8dea-52ba3440c01e",
                        "entry_id": "dff7969a-27d0-3249-987e-3f33953f3282",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "pétaudières"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                        "entry_id": "dff7969a-27d0-3249-987e-3f33953f3282",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Assemblée où il n’y a pas d’ordre, lieu où chacun veut commander. → voir anomie, confusion et désordre"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "69e4ff27-40ea-404f-a44f-23f0f2c22d4e",
                                "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                                "text": "C’est une agréable pétaudière où chacun est trop occupé et préoccupé des effets de son éloquence pour attacher beaucoup d’attention."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "acd7fa44-7c2d-4cc3-a315-bd2ad7eab5cf",
                                "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                                "text": "Je l’avais prédit dans le temps à Barras, qui voulut absolument se servir de ces conseils au lieu de les cisalpiner. Qu’en est-il résulté ? Ils se sont emparés du mouvement et ce mouvement n’a été en leurs mains qu’une pétaudière."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "349fe7c5-b9f3-4367-9462-cff55236f168",
                                "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                                "text": "Je décrivis la pétaudière qu’était la classe de dessin, et mon père m’apprit que c’était une tradition, justifiée par le fait que le silence n’est pas nécessaire pour dessiner."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5c399136-7e88-4578-8c63-d9ebc77533f6",
                                "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                                "text": "Mais la peur du contingent de 100 députés, toutefois, existe bel et bien. Pourquoi? Un gros caucus a tendance à se transformer en pétaudière."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f4036bc-dff5-4441-ad5e-54774387f547",
                                "sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                                "text": "\" cette année de cinquième s'annonce plaisante car nous avions fondé de grands espoirs sur le fait que nous allions la passer chez M.Bidart, dont la classe était une pétaudière.\""
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "4fdc3abf-c247-4e0a-b689-49ace60698a5",
                        "source_entry_id": "dff7969a-27d0-3249-987e-3f33953f3282",
                        "source_sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                        "target_lang_word": "balagan",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": []
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "51cf3fe8-326e-42ab-87d6-4e4593249e0f",
                        "source_entry_id": "dff7969a-27d0-3249-987e-3f33953f3282",
                        "source_sense_id": "de35319c-a5ae-323b-85a5-546ac35672db",
                        "target_lang_word": "bedlam",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bedlam",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "10bc4335-81ba-3520-b34e-c5b8bd16fef1",
                                        "entry_id": "d425671f-054f-32a2-9208-506f1229e4f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place or situation of chaotic uproar, and where confusion prevails."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11d404ea-7066-4d2a-9ae4-3ecfa4ce9028",
                                                "sense_id": "10bc4335-81ba-3520-b34e-c5b8bd16fef1",
                                                "text": "Some of the wards were veritable \"bedlams,\" and discharged patients have told of abuses practiced in them of which the mere recital causes a shudder."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2210ada9-a08f-4a7e-bf00-f077ce52fd60",
                                                "sense_id": "10bc4335-81ba-3520-b34e-c5b8bd16fef1",
                                                "text": "The outside of the Hyatt was bedlam. There was a group of more than a hundred injured people on the circular drive in front of the hotel."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c92ac1cb-3ce1-4707-bf10-c44ba3e9c95c",
                                                "sense_id": "10bc4335-81ba-3520-b34e-c5b8bd16fef1",
                                                "text": "A car was a rarity, and the sight of one in the distance was sometimes enough to cause bedlam during a class."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0af078cd-4375-496f-85de-3a3be360975e",
                                                "sense_id": "10bc4335-81ba-3520-b34e-c5b8bd16fef1",
                                                "text": "\"We had an extraordinary February half term - I think we had 22,000 visitors in the seven days. Which actually is a bit like bedlam at times.\""
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecbb2c0d-4184-337a-989d-34c4d528c724",
                                        "entry_id": "d425671f-054f-32a2-9208-506f1229e4f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An insane person; a lunatic; a madman."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d9516c3c-bafb-4a9e-a83d-9ba762da8b61",
                                                "sense_id": "ecbb2c0d-4184-337a-989d-34c4d528c724",
                                                "text": "Lets follow the old Earle, and get the bedlom\nTo lead him where he would, his rogiſh madnes\nAllows it ſelfe to any thing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93154361-a89b-4725-8be4-226a0641d812",
                                                "sense_id": "ecbb2c0d-4184-337a-989d-34c4d528c724",
                                                "text": "Firſt, The Pilgrims were cloathed with ſuch kind of Raiment, as was diverſe from the Raiment of any that Traded in that fair. The people therefore of the fair made a great gazing upon them: Some ſaid they were Fools, ſome they were Bedlams, and ſome they are Outlandiſh-men."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b4007cf5-c4fa-37cb-8a5a-b57c08ae2284",
                                        "entry_id": "d425671f-054f-32a2-9208-506f1229e4f6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A lunatic asylum; a madhouse."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0eb87ff5-89c5-4ad6-ac20-c7b4afb384db",
                                                "sense_id": "b4007cf5-c4fa-37cb-8a5a-b57c08ae2284",
                                                "text": "It was a ſhrewd ſaying of the old Monk, That two kind of Priſons would ſerve for all offenders in the World, an Inquiſition and a Bedlam: If any man ſhould deny the Being of a God and the Immortality of the Soul, ſuch a one ſhould be put into the firſt of these, the Inquiſition, as being a deſperate Heretick; but if any man ſhould profeſs to believe theſe things, and yet allow himſelf in any known wickedneſs, ſuch a one ſhould be put into Bedlam; becauſe there cannot be a greater folly and madneſs, than for a man in matters of greateſt moment and concernment to act againſt his beſt Reaſon and Underſtanding, and by his Life to contradict his Belief."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "484edb67-b410-416f-aa2d-8746dffba779",
                                                "sense_id": "b4007cf5-c4fa-37cb-8a5a-b57c08ae2284",
                                                "text": "Shut up the world at large, let Bedlam out;\nAnd you will be perhaps surprised to find\nAll things pursue exactly the same route,\nAs now with those of soi-disant sound mind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "fd000dae-1fea-49d8-89ae-003354fa61ea",
                                                "sense_id": "b4007cf5-c4fa-37cb-8a5a-b57c08ae2284",
                                                "text": "“There ’s another fellow,” muttered Scrooge; who overheard him: “my clerk, with fifteen shillings a-week, and a wife and family, talking about a merry Christmas. I ’ll retire to Bedlam.”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "270fda0e-7bbd-40ab-b497-89ad7e18e832",
                                                "sense_id": "b4007cf5-c4fa-37cb-8a5a-b57c08ae2284",
                                                "text": "Make a note of it: in man’s heaven there are no exercises for the intellect, nothing for it to live upon. It would rot there in a year—rot and stink. Rot and stink—and at that stage become holy. A blessed thing: only the holy can stand the joys of that bedlam."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
